WEBVTT

00:02:29.204 --> 00:02:30.496
The language isn't vivid.

00:02:30.496 --> 00:02:33.163
What we need is vivid language
that everyone gets.

00:02:33.163 --> 00:02:36.163
It's remarkable how many people
actually confuse climate change

00:02:36.163 --> 00:02:37.329
with the ozone hole.

00:02:37.371 --> 00:02:38.996
More than four in 10 Americans

00:02:39.038 --> 00:02:41.663
think the ozone hole
actually causes global warming.

00:02:41.663 --> 00:02:43.913
And so many of them remember
and understand

00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:46.079
so much about ozone depletion.

00:02:46.121 --> 00:02:47.246
Why is that?

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:49.829
Because it's a hole, it's a layer.

00:02:49.871 --> 00:02:52.704
People can see it,
imagine it, relate to it.

00:02:52.704 --> 00:02:55.954
It uses simple metaphor
that's an instant get.

00:02:55.954 --> 00:02:58.288
Here's a little story
that gets a similar "aha"

00:02:58.329 --> 00:02:59.538
for climate change.

00:02:59.538 --> 00:03:02.496
Humans have been on Earth
for about 300,000 years,